  "reason": "The best result so far is config_033 (0.7131 acc) using multimodal/multiprofile/scVI_n200/ResNet50/transformer/weighted. The image modality adds ~6% over the best RNA-only model (0.6530), yet ResNet50 alone scored only 0.2079, suggesting the image encoder's representational quality is a bottleneck. Config_039 makes a single clean change—swapping ResNet50 for the stronger imagenet_vit_l—while keeping all other validated-optimal settings (scVI_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted fusion). This directly tests whether a more powerful image encoder can push the multimodal model beyond 0.7131. As the final experiment, exploiting the strongest identified direction with the highest-potential single upgrade is the best use of the last budget slot."
}

